<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jovan Uglješa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1371">1371</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jovan Uglješa was a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who, with the title of despot, ruled the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serres">Serres</a> in eastern Macedonia from about 1365, after the Serbian Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> began to break up. With his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vukasin-mrnjavcevic">King Vukašin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prilep">Prilep</a> he led a campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1371, and both were killed when their army was destroyed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maritsa">Battle of the Maritsa</a> in September 1371.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jovan-uglesa.jpg" alt="Jovan Uglješa" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darko Nikolovski · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Most_na_umetnosta_$_(34).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
